-  
+## SSD-resident exact vectors
+
+The SSD targets keep MRQ metadata and binary codes in memory and refine candidates
+from the PCA-projected fvecs file:
+
+- MRQ reads all `D` exact dimensions from SSD.
+- MRQ+ keeps the first `B-1` exact dimensions and the full-vector norm in memory,
+  then reads only dimensions `[B-1, D)` from SSD.
+
+Build the dedicated targets and create both compact indexes:
+
+```bash
+cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+cmake --build build --target \
+  prepare_ssd_vectors res_ssd_index res_split_ssd_index \
+  res_ssd_search res_split_ssd_search -j
+
+# Convert the projected fvecs once. For D=1024 every vector is exactly one
+# aligned 4 KiB O_DIRECT record.
+build/src/prepare_ssd_vectors \
+  /data/msmarco/msmarco-qwen-1024_proj.fvecs \
+  /nvme/msmarco-qwen-1024_proj.ssdvec
+
+OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 build/src/res_ssd_index \
+  -d msmarco-qwen-1024 -s /data/msmarco/ -b 320 -c 4096
+OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 build/src/res_split_ssd_index \
+  -d msmarco-qwen-1024 -s /data/msmarco/ -b 320 -c 4096
+```
+
+Run the same `nprobe` sweep for MRQ and MRQ+. `direct` is the benchmark mode: it
+uses aligned `O_DIRECT` reads and therefore does not turn a warm page cache into
+an apparent SSD speedup.
+
+```bash
+OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 taskset -c 8 build/src/res_ssd_search \
+  -d msmarco-qwen-1024 -s /data/msmarco/ -r results/ \
+  -k 10 -b 320 -c 4096 --probes 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512 \
+  --rounds 3 --io-mode direct \
+  --vector-file /nvme/msmarco-qwen-1024_proj.ssdvec
+
+OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 taskset -c 8 build/src/res_split_ssd_search \
+  -d msmarco-qwen-1024 -s /data/msmarco/ -r results/ \
+  -k 10 -b 320 -c 4096 --probes 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512 \
+  --rounds 3 --io-mode direct \
+  --vector-file /nvme/msmarco-qwen-1024_proj.ssdvec
+```
+
+By default the exact vectors are read from `SOURCE/DATASET_proj.fvecs`, which
+is retained for compatibility and debugging. Direct-I/O benchmarks should use
+the page-aligned `.ssdvec` output via `--vector-file`; this avoids the 4100-byte
+fvecs record in 1024 dimensions crossing two pages. Dataset names that
+contain `msmarc` or `dbpedia` support 1024 dimensions and `B` values 128, 256,
+320, 384, 512, 640, 768, and 1024.
+
+Each run writes CSV columns for recall, search and end-to-end QPS, wall-clock
+latency, SSD reads/query, logical bytes, aligned submitted bytes, and time spent
+inside `pread`. `--io-mode buffered` is available for debugging only.
+
+Run the deterministic direct/buffered I/O regression test with:
+
+```bash
+bash test/RESQ/test_ssd.sh build
+```
 
 
